  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20345171",
      "title": "Handling CORS Errors",
      "lectureOrder": 535,
      "videoOrder": 474,
      "sourceHash": "7f38a93ed61c1640227608510d09c708958b509a52efbcb18f8d3cbacf793c11",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.29,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "So what's that CORS thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 6.61,
          "en": "and that course problem,?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.61,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "As I mentioned, I did already cover a CORS earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 12.47,
          "en": "in the course in their rest API section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.47,
          "end": 16.18,
          "en": "So there you'll all define that same information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.18,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "In the end CORS, short for cross original resource sharing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.59,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "is a security mechanism and forced by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.89,
          "end": 29.45,
          "en": "that makes sure that server A can't just send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.45,
          "end": 32.81,
          "en": "a request to server B and get data from it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.81,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "Server B instead needs to allow that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 37.42,
          "en": "So if you have a front end application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.42,
          "end": 39.64,
          "en": "running on server A, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.64,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "our react single page application running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 46.78,
          "en": "on local host 3000, and we have our other application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.78,
          "end": 48.5,
          "en": "our backend, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.5,
          "end": 52.24,
          "en": "running on server B in this case, our Rest API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.24,
          "end": 54.73,
          "en": "then the communication from A to B",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.73,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "will not be possible just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "By default browsers prevent GET, POST, PATCH",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 63.18,
          "en": "and so on requests, if frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.18,
          "end": 65.75,
          "en": "and backend server are not the same one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.75,
          "end": 69.76,
          "en": "And here on local host, even different ports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.76,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "imply different servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 76.52,
          "en": "So local host 3000 is not the same as local host 8,000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.57,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "Now this is a default security mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 81.86,
          "en": "however, we can tell the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.86,
          "end": 84.31,
          "en": "that we do want to allow access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.31,
          "end": 88.91,
          "en": "and we have to set this setting on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.91,
          "end": 90.95,
          "en": "where we do host the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.95,
          "end": 93.22999999999999,
          "en": "So on the backend, on the Rest API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.22999999999999,
          "end": 97.00999999999999,
          "en": "there, we can set specific response headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.00999999999999,
          "end": 100.86,
          "en": "to responses we sent back to the front end application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "that tell the browser that serves the front end application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 106.59,
          "en": "that getting that data is okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 109.59,
          "en": "and the front then should be able to proceed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "And it's really important to also keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "that this is just a browser security mechanism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "which is why we had no problems fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 119.95,
          "en": "and storing data with Postman.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.95,
          "end": 123.98,
          "en": "This simply doesn't care about this CORS thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.98,
          "end": 125.24,
          "en": "The browser does, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.24,
          "end": 127.8,
          "en": "and that's where we're getting a CORS error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.8,
          "end": 130.91,
          "en": "Now, how can we manipulate our Deno code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.91,
          "end": 135.73,
          "en": "to make sure that such requests are possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.73,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "Well, we need to switch to our Deno code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 140.25,
          "en": "and for that, I'm going to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "that my Deno extension is turned on again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 148.18,
          "en": "to ensure that I get proper IDE support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.18,
          "end": 152.06,
          "en": "and now here, on the backend and the backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.06,
          "end": 155.51,
          "en": "I wanna add a new middleware, which essentially makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.51,
          "end": 157.51,
          "en": "that every outgoing response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.51,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "has the proper headers attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "So for that here, we have our middleware function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 167.75,
          "en": "with context and next, and with the context object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.75,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "we can get access to the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 173.5,
          "en": "and there we can get access to our headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.5,
          "end": 176.39,
          "en": "And on this headers optic, there is a set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.39,
          "end": 180.35,
          "en": "to set a new header on that outgoing response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.35,
          "end": 183.43,
          "en": "And now there are three essential headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.43,
          "end": 186.93,
          "en": "which we should set on the outgoing responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 191.93,
          "en": "The first header is the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.86,
          "end": 196.94,
          "en": "This controls of whichever domains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.94,
          "end": 199.72,
          "en": "will be allowed to access our resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.72,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "And here we can set this to star,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 206.09,
          "en": "which means every domain is allowed to access our resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.09,
          "end": 208.8,
          "en": "So every other domain may send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 210.92000000000002,
          "en": "Of course, we could also restrict this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.92000000000002,
          "end": 212.103,
          "en": "to the domains we own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.97,
          "end": 216.28,
          "en": "The other important header, which we need to add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.28,
          "end": 220.38,
          "en": "the second important header, which we set in the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.38,
          "end": 225.38,
          "en": "is the Access-Control-Allow-Methods header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.5,
          "end": 228.94,
          "en": "This controls, which kind of HTTP methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.94,
          "end": 233.17000000000002,
          "en": "can be used for requests being sent to this backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.17000000000002,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "and here for this API, I want to allow get, post, put,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 242.21,
          "en": "and then also delete requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.21,
          "end": 245.51,
          "en": "because these are the four routes we registered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.51,
          "end": 249.74,
          "en": "So here we can add, get, post, put and delete",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.74,
          "end": 252.933,
          "en": "comma separated to allow for those requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 258.41,
          "en": "Now, the last header which we need to add with headers set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.41,
          "end": 263.41,
          "en": "is the Access-Control-Allow-Headers header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 268.87,
          "en": "This allows which headers may be set by the frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.87,
          "end": 270.69,
          "en": "when it requests data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 275.69,
          "en": "And there we should allow the content type header, why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.99,
          "end": 279.4,
          "en": "Because on the front end app, so in the frontend app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.4,
          "end": 281.8,
          "en": "under source components Todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.8,
          "end": 286.63,
          "en": "we can see that actually for put and for post requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.63,
          "end": 290.12,
          "en": "we do a set to content type two application Json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.12,
          "end": 292.7,
          "en": "this is important because this header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 292.7,
          "end": 296.2,
          "en": "on the request that's being sent to our Deno server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 296.2,
          "end": 299.57,
          "en": "will tell Deno and the Oak framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 299.57,
          "end": 302.57,
          "en": "that the data attached to this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.57,
          "end": 305.98,
          "en": "will be in the Json format and that matters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.98,
          "end": 308.57,
          "en": "because this allows Oak on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.57,
          "end": 310.51,
          "en": "to automatically parse that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.51,
          "end": 313.52,
          "en": "when we try to get access to the request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 313.52,
          "end": 316.02,
          "en": "So to get to this parsing and to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.02,
          "end": 319.43,
          "en": "that the incoming request data is transformed from Json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.43,
          "end": 322.307,
          "en": "to JavaScript object for that to happen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.307,
          "end": 325.59,
          "en": "we need to add the content type application Json header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.59,
          "end": 328.54,
          "en": "on the request sent from the frontend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.54,
          "end": 331.61,
          "en": "and that end turns there for something we need to allow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.61,
          "end": 334.1,
          "en": "with the appropriate CORS header here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.1,
          "end": 337.29,
          "en": "And with all of that, we of course need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.29,
          "end": 340.46,
          "en": "that they're after the next middleware in line is reached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.46,
          "end": 344.06,
          "en": "And we do this by calling next, but again, important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 344.06,
          "end": 346.73,
          "en": "I mentioned it in the last course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 346.73,
          "end": 350.19,
          "en": "in the Oak framework, you should await next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 350.19,
          "end": 352.69,
          "en": "and there for add async here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.69,
          "end": 356.2,
          "en": "If the next middleware in line is a synchronous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.2,
          "end": 359.51,
          "en": "and our route middlewares will be asynchronous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.51,
          "end": 363.68,
          "en": "because our route middlewares do use async keyword as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.68,
          "end": 365.62,
          "en": "we do have promises in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 365.62,
          "end": 368.52,
          "en": "So we should await for those actions to complete",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 368.52,
          "end": 370.48,
          "en": "before the response is sent back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 370.48,
          "end": 373.85,
          "en": "and we do this by awaiting next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 373.85,
          "end": 377.47,
          "en": "With this out of the way, we can restart our backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 377.47,
          "end": 379.75,
          "en": "by repeating does run command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 379.75,
          "end": 383.4,
          "en": "And if we now go back to the client site application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 383.4,
          "end": 385.81,
          "en": "and we reload local host 3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 385.81,
          "end": 387.713,
          "en": "you see the error here has gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 388.68,
          "end": 392.6,
          "en": "And if we now add Todo, learn Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 392.6,
          "end": 394.14300000000003,
          "en": "this is being added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 395.46,
          "end": 397.90999999999997,
          "en": "If you click edit, it's loaded here for editing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 397.90999999999997,
          "end": 400.55,
          "en": "and I can add more exclamation marks for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 400.55,
          "end": 402.3,
          "en": "and here we go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.3,
          "end": 405.87,
          "en": "I can add another Todo like also learn Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 405.87,
          "end": 407.57,
          "en": "and that's gonna also edit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 407.57,
          "end": 409.8,
          "en": "And of course I can also delete a Todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.8,
          "end": 412.89,
          "en": "if I reload the app that also is maintained.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.89,
          "end": 415.39,
          "en": "Of course, if I ever shut down the backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 415.39,
          "end": 417.2,
          "en": "all the data is lost though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 417.2,
          "end": 421.39,
          "en": "because we currently still only save our data in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 421.39,
